WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000 line:0 size:90% align:center
An incoming impactor. An early Earth impact concentrates energy at the surface.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000 line:0 size:90% align:center
Impact and excavation. Shock, fragmentation and excavation displace target material.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000 line:0 size:90% align:center
Ejecta settles. Excavated material accumulates outside the crater.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000 line:0 size:90% align:center
A simple crater. The depression and raised rim record impact; later erosion can remove them.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.000 line:0 size:90% align:center
Evidence, not a clock. Crater relations give relative order; isotopic ages add numerical constraints.
